ework in Lean 4 with Mathlib, proving 15 new theorems including the autocorrela
tion symmetry, the Parseval identity for difference sets, Fermat's sum-of-two-s
quares theorem for light primes, and concrete coherence comparisons between lig
ht and dark prime sets. Computational experiments across 4, 5, 6, and 8-element
 prime sets consistently show that light primes have lower autocorrelation ener
gy than dark primes, supporting the hypothesis that their Gaussian integer spli
tting distributes additive structure more uniformly. All proofs are machine-ver
ified with zero remaining sorries.[] 
