of the Brazilian mathematician Imre Simon. Despite sounding like a mathematical
 joke, tropical algebra turned out to be astonishingly powerful. It simplified 
problems in algebraic geometry, helped biologists build evolutionary trees, and
 even improved scheduling algorithms for airlines.[] 
