[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/12 The mathematical landscape is rich with *convergence* results
  theorems guaranteeing that iterative processes reach stable states. The Knast
er-Tarski theorem shows that every monotone function on a complete lattice has 
a least fixed point. The Banach contraction principle shows that contractive ma
ps on complete metric spaces converge to unique fixed points. Lawvere's fixed p
oint theorem demonstrates that surjective point-mappings force universal fixed 
points.[] 
 []


