s sums of two squares and split in the Gaussian integers, and *dark primes* ( 3
 mod 4), which remain inert. We prove that these two classes partition all odd 
primes, that prime gaps grow without bound (the "expansion of space"), that eve
ry integer > 1 participates in this light/dark duality through its prime factor
ization, and that the composite gaps between primes can be made arbitrarily lar
ge with actual prime endpoints. All 18 main theorems are machine-verified with 
no axioms beyond the standard foundations (propext, Classical.choice, Quot.soun
d).[] 
