Overfull \hbox (2887.70876pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 46192--46192
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/12 **SAT** asks: given a logical formula with many variables, ca
n you find values that make it true? It's the original NP-complete problem  eve
ry hard search problem can be translated into SAT. The oracle framework defines
 a "cost function" that counts how many clauses in the formula are violated. A 
satisfying assignment is one where the cost hits zero. The researchers formally
 prove: *the cost is zero if and only if every clause is satisfied*  a statemen
t that sounds obvious but, when machine-verified, provides an unshakeable found
ation.[] 
 []

