[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/12 **Factoring** asks: given a large number N, find two numbers 
that multiply to give N. This problem guards your credit card number every time
 you shop online (RSA encryption). The oracle framework defines a "tropical act
ion"  the distance |N  a×b| between the target and a candidate product. A valid
 factorization is one where this tropical action vanishes. Again, formally prov
ed: *the action is zero if and only if a×b = N.*[] 
 []

