[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/12 **Disguise 1  Geometry.** Divide by $c^2$: the point $(a/c,\,
 b/c)$ sits exactly on the unit circle. The triple $(3, 4, 5)$ becomes $(0.6, 0
.8)$. Every Pythagorean triple is a rational point on a perfect circle.[] 
 []

