[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/12 **Abstract:** We continue the investigation of four-channel i
nteger signatures (n) = (n, r(n), r(n), r(n)), where r(n) counts representation
s of n as a sum of k squares. Building on 22 theorems from Session 1, we establ
ish 19 new machine-verified theorems in Lean 4, run 12 computational experiment
s covering multiplicativity, entropy hierarchies, and prime power structure, an
d discover several new results. Our key findings include: (1) the complete char
acterization of powers-of-2 signatures, showing that r(2) = 4 and r(2) = 24 are
 constant while r(2) grows exponentially; (2) the formal verification of Euler'
s four-square identity (quaternion norm multiplicativity); (3) the Eisenstein n
orm connection p²  p + 1 governing channel ratios; and (4) a strict entropy hie
rarchy H(N) < H(N) < H(N) confirmed computationally to N = 5000. All theorems a
re verified by Lean's kernel, providing mathematical certainty beyond peer revi
ew.[] 
 []


