[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/12 Recent interest in applying machine learning and GPU computin
g to mathematical problems has inspired several proposals for neural or gradien
t-based factoring algorithms. The "Neuromorphic Inside-Out Factoring" (IOF) alg
orithm examined here represents one such approach: it initializes millions of "
neurons" as random values `k  [0, 1]`, optimizes them using Adam with a custom 
loss function, and periodically checks whether any neuron position yields a non
trivial `gcd(4k²  1, N)`.[] 
 []


