ren matrices (B and B) are **unipotent**  they satisfy (B  I)³ = 0. In the lang
uage of relativity, they are "null rotations," the discrete analogues of boosts
 along a light ray. The third matrix B is fundamentally different: it's a refle
ction with determinant 1.[] 
