[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/12 **The Riemann Hypothesis.** Which prime numbers can be hypote
nuses of Pythagorean triples? The answer, proved by Fermat in the 17th century,
 is: exactly the primes that leave a remainder of 1 when divided by 4. So 5 (= 
3² + 4²), 13 (= 5² + 12²), 17, 29, 37, 41 are all "hypotenuse primes," while 3,
 7, 11, 19, 23 are not.[] 
